   "body_html": "You need to post code that illustrates the problem you mention in the last para."
  },
  {
   "post_type": "comment",
   "post_id": 2680224,
   "parent_id": 2662652,
   "parent_type": "question",
   "author_user_id": 141349,
   "author_display_name": "Ernelli",
   "author_id_missing": false,
   "role": "responder",
   "is_accepted": null,
   "permalink": "https://stackoverflow.com/questions/2662652/#comment2680224_2662652",
   "score": 0,
   "created_utc": "2010-04-18T15:19:12Z",
   "edited": false,
   "license": "CC BY-SA 2.5",
   "body_html": "You can only call free on memory obtained using malloc, calloc, realloc. Some functions return data that should be free&#39;d as well, such as strdup. But getenv does not allocate any data to be freed by caller. <a href=\"http://www.manpagez.com/man/3/getenv/\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">manpagez.com/man/3/getenv</a>"
  },
